  "name": "Turn Google Trends into Instagram and TikTok image posts with GPT Image and PostWire",
  "tags": [],
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "66061ccf-3a87-4e86-a8ae-edd73a199493",
      "name": "Sticky Note",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -643,
        -121
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 520,
        "height": 803,
        "content": "## Turn Google Trends into on-brand image posts\nEvery morning OpenAI picks the one Google Trends search your brand can join, GPT Image makes the visual, and PostWire posts it to Instagram, TikTok (photo mode) and Facebook, each with its own caption.\n\n### How it works\n1. **Every morning at 8:00** reads the Google Trends RSS feed for your country (free, no key) and **Skip trends already used** drops any trend seen on a previous day.\n2. **Pick a trend with OpenAI** returns the trend that fits your brand, an image prompt and a caption per network. It skips tragedies, politics and private people; when nothing fits, nothing is posted.\n3. **Generate the image with GPT Image** creates a square image that goes straight to a PostWire upload slot (PNG is converted to JPEG for Instagram and TikTok).\n4. **Publish with PostWire** posts it everywhere. The date and trend are the idempotency key, so a retry never posts twice.\n5. Every run is logged in Google Sheets with the post links; when a network refuses, **Gmail** emails you the fix.\n\n### Setup\n1. Create a free account at postwire.io, connect your networks and copy your API key. In n8n add a **Header Auth** credential (name `Authorization`, value `Bearer pw_live_\u2026`) and select it in the three PostWire nodes.\n2. Fill in **Set your brand and niche**: brand, niche, country code (US, GB, DE...) and networks.\n3. Add an OpenAI credential (the image is about one cent with gpt-image-1-mini).\n4. Create a sheet with the columns date, trend, angle, status, links and note, and pick it in both Sheets nodes. Connect Gmail and put your address in **Email me the fix**.\n\n### Customize\nChange the hour in the trigger, or the safety rules in the OpenAI system message."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
